<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to the Blood Death Knight DPS Guide!  This guide will cover current everything from opener, rotation, and gearing options. A heavily requested guide, but not able to come into it's own until recently. Blizzard has changed it's viewpoint recently of leaving Classic as it was back in the day and started to address some issues and concerns of classes to improve the gameplay for the players. You see this with a Retribution Paladin and Feral Druid Buff, or with Ignite and Deep Wounds munching. They've also chosen to address some of the scaling issues of the signature Blood talent  <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>. Resulting in not an exactly 50% damage as the tooltip suggests due to it not inheriting some of the stats your character has, but it's a lot closer than it was. This isn't a massive dps increase for Blood, it's barely any change at all. There's been a lot of interest about Blood, and if you would like more complex answers to questions like the double disease opener then join us at  <a href="https://discord.gg/7hYVEz7aS9" target="_blank">Woims Discord</a> or <a href="https://discord.gg/ebonhold" target="_blank">Ebon Hold (Fonsas') Discord</a>.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="class-overview">
<span class="c6">Class Overview for Blood Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King</span></h2>Often shunned by the community, Blood is coming together as the expansion goes on. With Armor Penetration becoming more prevalent in gear, Blood inches closer to the damage of Frost or Unholy DPS. Not quite there in Ulduar, you see it get a lot closer in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>. My big disclaimer is, Blood is not the best DPS spec for Death Knights - if you can play all the specs at a high level, it would be a raid dps loss to play Blood over Unholy or Frost even in ICC BIS due to the lack of AOE damage. If you're in a casual guild, not speed running, or allowed to play whatever you want and you've wanted to play Blood then do it. Getting acquainted with the spec will help you as you move into the next phases of Classic where Blood starts to get even stronger. Most of Classic has turned into a hyper optimization of the game that has woven itself into even the most casual of guilds, heroic dungeons, and world content. We've seen countless tiers that this is not needed to do a majority of content. This is the only expansion where Blood DPS is a thing, so if you want to relive some fond memories and play something less optimal then do it. <br/>
<br/>Blood is heavily gear dependent, don't expect to go into a raid with mediocre gear and being in top 5 DPS on a boss. In order for you to justify playing Blood, you need to be able to compete with other classes and not be a hindrance to the raid. It's worth noting that Blood is the easiest of the 3 DPS specs to play for Death Knights and if you have the BIS gear, you might see some higher performance than the other specs if you cannot play them properly and kill times favor you. Blood DPS suffers the same way that Blood tanking does, in that AOE is virtually nonexistent. When comparing the other 2 DPS specs to Blood in this regard, you will not even seen close to equal damage numbers overall. Blood is strictly a Single Target and 2 Target spec, keep this mind when comparing the specs.<div class="pad"></div>
<hr/>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="mechanics">
<span class="c6">Class Mechanics for Blood Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="presences">Presences</h5>All <span class="c6">Death Knights</span> have three different Presences to choose from. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48266/blood-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bloodpresence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Presence</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48263/frost-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_frostpresence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Presence</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48265/unholy-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_unholypresence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Presence</span></a>. You will be sitting in Blood Presence Presence. It grants 15% increased damage, and healing you for 4% of your direct damage dealt.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="runes">Runes</h5>The core of the Death Knight class, there are four types of Runes, Blood, Unholy, Frost, and Death. Baseline you'll start with two Blood, two Frost, and two Unholy runes. The majority of your abilities and attacks require some combination of these runes. Please note, that abilities that require one Rune grant only 10 RP. Your abilities will use the first available rune in its grouping.<br/>
<br/>Runes regenerate after use at a rate of ten seconds each, with what's called a "Rune Grace Period." During the Rune Grace Period you'll receive a reduction of up to 2.5 seconds in the regeneration time of your runes, based on the delay with which you use them after they are refreshed. As an example, if a Rune regenerates, and you use the same global cooldown on a Blood Rune, or spending Runic Power, if you immediately use an ability or spell that uses that Rune, the Rune(s) you used for it will be set to a 8.5 second cooldown. This Grace Period caps at 2.5 seconds.<h6 class="heading-size-6" id="death-runes">Death Runes</h6>If you have no regular runes available, Death Runes will be consumed in the order of what the Rune was before it was converted. Death Rune generation for Blood DPS is very good. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50034/death-rune-mastery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Rune Mastery</span></a> means every time you use <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49924/death-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_butcher2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Strike</span></a> then those runes spent will come back as Death Runes. These Death Runes will then be used for more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55262/heart-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart Strike</span></a>'s. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=45529/blood-tap">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bloodtap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Tap</span></a> allows you to convert a Blood Rune into a Death Rune for 20 seconds, every 1 minute. This essentially breaks down to a 40 second cooldown, as the ability goes on cooldown the moment it is used, and the Blood Tap buff lasts for 20 seconds. This ability does not require you to have a Blood Rune active, and it also grants 10 RP. If you have 2 Blood Runes, both active or both inactive, it will convert one to a Death Rune and activate it.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="runic-power">Runic Power</h5>Runic Power is considered the 'Spender' resource for Death Knights of all specializations, the baseline being a pool of 100. Your abilities that cost one Rune of any type will provide a baseline of 10 Runic Power, abilities that cost two and three Runes of any type will provide 15 Runic Power.<div class="pad"></div>
<hr/>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="strengths-weaknesses">
<span class="c6">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses for Blood Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="strengths">Strengths</h5>
<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strong Single Target damage</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strong burst through the use of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Brings <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53138/abominations-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_intensifyrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Abomination's Might</span></a> if you don't have an Enhancement Shaman or Marksman Hunter</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Decent self-sustain due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49924/death-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_butcher2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Strike</span></a> being a core part of the rotation.</div></li></ul>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="weaknesses">Weaknesses</h5>
<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Lack Luster AOE damage</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Some of the worst Mobility the game has</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Heavily gear Dependent</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Worms eats some healing</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Community Perception</div></li></ul>
